---
/**
 * foodcraft / PageBL — "Kalinaw Coffee" (a café that roasts its own).
 *
 * Cream & rust: Fraunces display over Space Grotesk body on a warm cream
 * ground, with a rust accent, pill controls, and two ESPRESSO bands that carry
 * an amber accent of their own. The signature is the ITALIC RUST EMPHASIS
 * inside a headline — "Slow mornings, <em>strong coffee.</em>" — and the ARCH
 * on the hero photograph (200px 200px 14px 14px), which is the one shape in the
 * template that is not a rectangle.
 *
 * THE DESIGN IS THE SPECIFICATION. Every value below is lifted verbatim from
 * "Kalinaw Coffee Landing.dc.html". Nothing is re-derived, darkened or "made
 * portable". The one axis the design itself exposes as configurable is its
 * accent — its own data-props offers a colour picker seeded #B4541F — so that
 * is the token the theme engine is welcome to move.
 *
 * WHY --ink IS BOTH TEXT AND A BAND, and why that is fine here. #241A12 is the
 * body colour AND the ground of the Trust strip and the How band. On the Kubo
 * Stays template an equivalent overload was a bug, because there the shared
 * colour was an ACCENT: remapping it moved a band and a word independently and
 * one of them always broke. Here the pair is ink/paper, which every scheme
 * remaps together and coherently — a dark scheme gives light text on dark
 * bands, which is the same design inverted rather than a different one. So
 * --ink and --paper are used as the engine's own vocabulary, deliberately.
 *
 * WHAT IS *NOT* THE ENGINE'S: --band-accent (#E8A33C), the amber. It appears
 * ONLY on the espresso bands — the eyebrow, the step discs, the band button —
 * where it was chosen against #241A12 specifically, so it is the one colour on
 * the page that MUST NOT move when an admin picks a scheme. The same goes for
 * --band and its three variants and --bone and its two, which exist only on
 * those bands.
 *
 * IT IS CALLED --band-accent BECAUSE IT CANNOT BE CALLED --amber. The first cut
 * of this file named it --amber and claimed in this very paragraph that the
 * engine knew nothing about it. genericThemeOverrides.ts:295 emits
 * `--amber: <palette.primary> !important`, so the claim was false and every
 * scheme pick would have repainted the band eyebrow, the step discs and the
 * band button — on the maroon scheme, #800000 on #241A12, which is barely
 * visible. An audit pass caught it by reading the engine rather than the
 * comment. Before naming any new token, grep genericThemeOverrides.ts for it:
 * the engine owns a long list of colour words (gold peach amber lime blue mint
 * yellow teal forest olive brass) and silently wins every one with !important.
 *
 * WHAT THE ENGINE DOES OWN HERE, deliberately: --paper --paper-2 --card --ink
 * --ink-soft --line --accent --accent-deep --muted and the rgb triplets. Those
 * are the axes a scheme SHOULD move. Note --muted among them: it is remapped to
 * palette.inkSoft, so the contrast figure below is the native value, not a
 * guarantee under every scheme.
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: the wrapper emits the WHOLE document (doctype, head,
 * tokens, fonts, Leaflet, skip link, scroll-reveal). It does NOT compose with
 * BaseLayout. It is the only file in the variant that touches `siteData`; the
 * 15 section components receive only `layout` + `content`.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. PageBL renders no editable text of
 * its own — it READS layout.businessName / layout.tagline (<title>),
 * content.description (<meta name="description">), layout.favicon and
 * layout.ogImage || layout.favicon. Every data-field / data-image-field /
 * data-href-field hook lives in a section component.
 *
 * THE ONE HARDCODED VISIBLE STRING is the skip link's "Skip to content". It is
 * an a11y affordance, visible on focus only.
 *
 * VERIFIED CONTRAST — COMPUTED from the hexes declared below (sRGB relative
 * luminance, WCAG 2.x), not estimated. An earlier draft of this table stated
 * several pairs HIGHER than the palette actually gives, which is the dangerous
 * direction: it can wave through a pair that is under the bar. Re-run the
 * arithmetic if you touch a hex.
 *   ink/paper 16.65 · ink/paper-2 14.93 · ink/card 17.05 · ink/well 14.06
 *   ink-soft/paper 6.28 · accent/paper 4.85 (eyebrows, numerals, rules)
 *   paper on an accent fill 4.85 · bone/ink 15.83 · band-accent/ink 7.91
 *   ink on a band-accent fill 7.91 · bone-soft/ink 7.31 · bone-soft-2/ink 9.46
 *   muted/paper 3.56 — BELOW AA, the design's own value, used only on 10-13px
 *   labels that the heading beside them repeats. Darkening --muted to #7C6C5C
 *   takes it to 4.93 and is a one-line change; it is the owner's palette and
 *   the owner's call, so the file ships the design's.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES here (read lib/genericThemeOverrides.ts before adding a
 * button anywhere): .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta
 * .nav-right .testi .cta-band .trust, and `.hero` on a <section>. The engine
 * pins those labels with !important for every state. Buttons here are
 * .btn--fill / .btn--line / .btn--band-accent / .linkc, which it does not touch.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL (two lines, wrapper-local, touches no shared file):
 * lib/astro-builder.ts defaults `layout.fontPairing` to the literal 'modern',
 * and resolveTheme's `lockVariant` only blanks ''/'auto'/'default' — so without
 * the sentinel buildOverrideCss force-swaps Fraunces + Space Grotesk with
 * !important on ~every real site and the design's faces never reach a visitor.
 * We treat astro-builder's DEFAULT as unset; a deliberate admin pick applies.
 *
 * RENDER ORDER, exactly as the design draws it: Header, Hero, Trust, About (our
 * story), Services (the menu), Why (why here), Gallery, How, Testimonials,
 * Credentials, Location (visit us), Area (delivery & catering), Faq, CtaBand,
 * Footer.
 *
 * BANDS: a section that wants the espresso ground carries `band-dark` alongside
 * its own class. That one class flips the h2, the body copy, the eyebrow and
 * both button treatments — a section must not restate them.
 *
 * Leaflet: this wrapper LOADS leaflet.css + leaflet.js and defines
 * window.__foodcraftBLInitMap (family-unique, because a preview harness can
 * render two wrappers in one document and a shared name cross-wires the maps).
 * LocationBL calls that exact string. Keep `el.innerHTML = ''` in the boot — it
 * is what erases the drawn fallback map-face — and keep id="map" literal.
 */
import HeaderBL from './header/HeaderBL.astro';
import HeroBL from './hero/HeroBL.astro';
import TrustBL from './trust/TrustBL.astro';
import AboutBL from './about/AboutBL.astro';
import ServicesBL from './services/ServicesBL.astro';
import WhyBL from './why/WhyBL.astro';
import GalleryBL from './gallery/GalleryBL.astro';
import HowBL from './how/HowBL.astro';
import TestimonialsBL from './testimonials/TestimonialsBL.astro';
import CredentialsBL from './credentials/CredentialsBL.astro';
import LocationBL from './location/LocationBL.astro';
import AreaBL from './area/AreaBL.astro';
import FaqBL from './faq/FaqBL.astro';
import CtaBandBL from './ctaBand/CtaBandBL.astro';
import FooterBL from './footer/FooterBL.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
// FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL — see the note in the frontmatter.
const __pairing = (layout.fontPairing === 'modern' && !layout.fontPairingExplicit) ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__pairing);
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __pairing);
const __desc = (content as any).description || '';
const __favicon = layout.favicon || '';
const __og = layout.ogImage || layout.favicon || '';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-PH" data-page="BL">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<title>{title}</title>
{__desc && <meta name="description" content={__desc} />}
<meta name="theme-color" content="#FFFCF6" />
<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
{__desc && <meta property="og:description" content={__desc} />}
{__og && <meta property="og:image" content={__og} />}
{__favicon && <link rel="icon" href={__favicon} />}

<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,600;1,9..144,500&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
{__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
<!-- Leaflet. BOTH tags are load-bearing: without the stylesheet the tiles
     render as a stack of unpositioned images, and without the script window.L
     never exists, the boot below returns immediately, and LocationBL's drawn
     fallback map-face is all an owner ever sees however many coordinates they
     type. scripts/check-template-blocks.mjs fails a wrapper that defines a map
     boot without loading both. -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />

<style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Every selector is prefixed html[data-page="BL"], including the reset,
       body, img, a and ::selection, so nothing leaks into a sister wrapper
       built in the same run — and nothing leaks in. An unscoped rule in one of
       these blocks reaches all 63 templates: two of them once shipped
       h1,h2,h3,h4{text-transform:uppercase} and capitalised every mixed-case
       design in the catalogue.

       (Never write a literal end-style-tag inside this block, comments
        included — it is an HTML raw-text element, so the parser would end the
        stylesheet right there.)
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BL"] {
      /* ── the light world ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      --paper: #FFFCF6;
      --paper-2: #F7EFE1;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --well: #F2E8D8;
      --ink: #241A12;
      --ink-soft: #6B5C4E;
      --muted: #948373;
      --line: #E9DFCF;
      --line-2: #EDE2D1;
      --line-3: #F2EADC;
      --line-btn: #E0D3C0;

      /* ── the accent, and the ONE token the engine may move ────────────── */
      --accent: #B4541F;
      --accent-deep: #8E3F14;
      --accent-rgb: 180,84,31;

      /* ── the espresso bands. --band-accent and the bones exist ONLY here, chosen
            against #241A12, and the engine does not know them — so a scheme
            pick recolours the rust and leaves these legible. ─────────────── */
      --band: #241A12;
      --band-deep: #1C130C;
      --band-well: #2A1E14;
      --band-rule: #3A2C20;
      --band-accent: #E8A33C;
      --bone: #FBF6EC;
      --bone-soft: #B8A795;
      --bone-soft-2: #CDBFAD;
      --bone-rgb: 251,246,236;

      /* ── engine vocabulary it also rewrites; declared so nothing inherits a
            blank, and used deliberately (see the note in the frontmatter). */
      --ink-rgb: 36,26,18;
      --paper-rgb: 255,252,246;
      --on-ink: #FBF6EC;
      --on-paper: #241A12;
      --on-accent: #FFFCF6;
      --on-primary: #FFFCF6;

      /* ── type + metrics ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      --disp: "Fraunces", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --serif: "Fraunces", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --sans: "Space Grotesk", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      /* This design has no monospace: its tracked caps are Space Grotesk 600. */
      --mono: "Space Grotesk", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --maxw: 1240px;
      /* Rounded, not sharp: 100px pills on every control, 14–16px on cards and
         plates. The hero's arch (200px 200px 14px 14px) is the one exception
         and belongs to HeroBL. */
      --r-pill: 100px;
      --r-lg: 16px;
      --r-md: 14px;
    }

    /* ── reset + document ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BL"] *,
    html[data-page="BL"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BL"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BL"] {
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; scroll-behavior: smooth;
      /* The header is sticky and ~74px tall; without this every in-page anchor
         lands with the top of its section underneath it. */
      scroll-padding-top: 88px;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BL"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BL"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.7;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] img { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
    html[data-page="BL"] a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    html[data-page="BL"] ::selection { background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }
    /* text-transform is DECLARED, not defaulted. A property a template never
       states is one another template's is:global block can reach. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink);
      letter-spacing: 0; line-height: 1.08; text-transform: none;
    }
    /* This bare-element paragraph reset is (0,1,1): always qualify a section's
       own paragraph rules with a parent class so they win. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(p) { margin: 0 0 1em; }

    /* ── layout scaffolding ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.wrap) { width: min(var(--maxw), 92vw); margin-inline: auto; }
    html[data-page="BL"] section { padding: clamp(56px,7.6vw,96px) 0; position: relative; }

    /* ── THE ESPRESSO BAND. One class, and it flips everything a section would
          otherwise have to restate. The eyebrow becomes AMBER, which is the
          design's own choice and the only place amber appears. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) { background-color: var(--band); color: var(--bone); }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .h2,
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .fig { color: var(--bone); }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .kick { color: var(--band-accent); }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .body,
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .lede { color: var(--bone-soft); }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .mono { color: var(--bone-soft-2); }
    /* On the band the italic emphasis becomes amber — rust on espresso is 3.43:1
       and would delete the emphasised words. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .h2 em,
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .h2 .em { color: var(--band-accent); }

    /* ── .kick — the eyebrow. 10px caps at .42em, rust on cream (4.85:1). */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.kick) {
      /* line-height pinned TIGHT for the same reason as .btn. This eyebrow
         carries no rule under it — that is the next template in the family —
         so nothing here comes adrift; what a loose line box does is inflate
         the eyebrow's own box and push the headline further down than the
         design draws it. */
      line-height: 1.1;
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: .42em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent);
    }

    /* ── display headline + the ITALIC RUST EMPHASIS (the design's signature).
          Fraunces ships a real italic at weight 500, so this is not synthesised.
          Sections feed the h2 with set:html so an owner can place the emphasis
          anywhere in their own sentence. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.h2) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400;
      font-size: clamp(31px,4vw,54px); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: 0;
      margin: 0 0 .3em; color: var(--ink); max-width: 24ch;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.h2 em),
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.h2 .em),
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.em) { font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; color: var(--accent); }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.lede) {
      color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(15.5px,1.5vw,17.5px); line-height: 1.72;
      max-width: 44ch; margin: 0;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.body) {
      color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(14.5px,1.3vw,15px); line-height: 1.75;
    }
    /* ── .mono — small tracked caps. --muted is the design's value; see the
          contrast note in the frontmatter. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.mono) {
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 500; font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: .2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
    }
    /* ── .fig — the serif figure (prices, proof numbers, numerals). */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.fig) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums; line-height: 1;
    }
    /* ── .chip — the hero's tag pills and any other outlined label. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.chip) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft);
      border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-pill);
      padding: 7px 14px;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .chip {
      color: var(--bone-soft-2); border-color: rgba(var(--bone-rgb),.28);
    }

    /* ── BUTTONS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       Straight from the design's own renderVals():
         .btn--fill    btnNav/btnLg — rust fill, #FFFCF6 label, pill
         .btn--line    the outlined secondary — white fill, hairline, ink label
         .btn--band-accent   btnAmber — amber fill, espresso label, used ON the bands
       Every hover DARKENS the same fill and keeps the same label colour: never
       lighter, never transparent, never a hue change. That is what stranded the
       Ironwood label, and the same trap is live here because buildOverrideCss
       pins some labels with !important. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn) {
      /* DECLARED, not left to chance. A button with no background of its own
         is filled by whatever rule lands last, and index.astro bundles every
         template's is:global CSS onto every page — so an unscoped
         `.btn { background: var(--ink) }` from another family was painting
         this family's outline controls. The variants below each set their
         own fill; this is what the ones that want none actually get. */
      background-color: transparent;
      /* line-height is DECLARED. The design sets none on its buttons, so they
         render at the browser normal; inheriting body-'s 1.7 instead inflated
         every control by ~6px. (An earlier draft added "and pushed the eyebrow's
         underline off its text" — that is the NEXT template in this family. This
         eyebrow has no rule under it; see the note on .kick above.) A label is
         one line: 1 is what a button wants. */
      line-height: 1;
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .55em;
      padding: 16px 32px; min-height: 48px;
      border-radius: var(--r-pill); border: 1px solid transparent;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none;
      cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;
      transition: background-color .18s ease, box-shadow .18s ease, transform .18s ease, border-color .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--fill) {
      background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); border-color: var(--accent);
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) {
      background-color: var(--accent-deep); color: var(--on-accent); border-color: var(--accent-deep);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--fill:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    /* The design's secondary: a white fill inside a warm hairline. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--line) {
      background-color: var(--card); color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--line-btn);
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--line:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--bone); border-color: var(--ink);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--line:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    /* Amber on espresso, 7.91:1. The design uses it for the band's one action. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--band-accent) {
      background-color: var(--band-accent); color: var(--band); border-color: var(--band-accent);
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--band-accent:hover) {
      background-color: var(--band-accent); color: var(--band); border-color: var(--band-accent);
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 999px rgba(0,0,0,.14);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn--band-accent:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    /* Inside a band the outlined secondary takes bone, not ink. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .btn--line {
      background-color: transparent; color: var(--bone); border-color: rgba(var(--bone-rgb),.4);
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) .btn--line:hover {
      background-color: rgba(var(--bone-rgb),.12); color: var(--bone); border-color: var(--bone);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BL"] .btn { transition: none; }
      html[data-page="BL"] .btn--fill:hover,
      html[data-page="BL"] .btn--line:hover,
      html[data-page="BL"] .btn--band-accent:hover { transform: none; }
    }

    /* ── .linkc — the quiet text action (the footer's "Message us →"). Its
          colour never changes on hover, only the rule under it, so it cannot
          fail a contrast check mid-interaction. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.linkc) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .5em; min-height: 44px;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px;
      letter-spacing: .02em; color: var(--accent);
      border-bottom: 1px solid transparent; padding-bottom: 2px;
      transition: border-bottom-color .18s ease, transform .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.linkc:hover) {
      color: var(--accent); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); transform: translateY(-1px);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BL"] .linkc { transition: none; } }

    /* ── FOCUS · one DUO ring: a 3px paper outline inside a rust halo, so it
          reads on cream, on a rust fill and over a photograph alike. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(a,button,summary,[tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--paper); outline-offset: 0;
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--accent);
      border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.band-dark) :where(a,button,summary,[tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline-color: var(--band); box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--band-accent);
    }

    /* ── .plate / .ph — the image frame and its empty state. The design's wells
          are flat --well; the two faint washes only exist so an unfilled slot
          reads as a deliberate surface rather than a broken image. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.plate) {
      position: relative; overflow: hidden; min-height: 180px;
      border-radius: var(--r-md);
      background-color: var(--well); isolation: isolate;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.plate) .ph {
      position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1;
      background-color: var(--well);
      background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-repeat: no-repeat;
      background-image:
        radial-gradient(78% 64% at 22% 14%, rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.14), transparent 62%),
        radial-gradient(66% 60% at 84% 90%, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.07), transparent 60%);
      transition: transform .5s ease;
    }
    /* Caption on an OPAQUE espresso pill, never a gradient scrim: bone on
       espresso holds 15.83:1 over ANY owner photo, however dark or blown out. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.plate) .cap {
      position: absolute; left: 12px; bottom: 12px; z-index: 3;
      max-width: calc(100% - 24px);
      background-color: var(--band); color: var(--bone);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 9px;
      letter-spacing: .2em; text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: var(--r-pill);
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BL"] :where(.plate) .ph { transition: none; } }

    /* ── .rowrule — the label/value hairline row used by the spec ledger, the
          opening hours and the delivery list. One declaration, three sections. */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.rowrule) {
      display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px;
      padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2);
      min-width: 0;
    }

    /* ── scroll reveal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.reveal) {
      opacity: 0; transform: translateY(14px);
      transition: opacity .6s ease, transform .6s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.reveal.in) { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="1"]) { transition-delay: .08s; }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="2"]) { transition-delay: .16s; }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="3"]) { transition-delay: .24s; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BL"] .reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none !important; }
    }

    /* ── skip link ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent);
      padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 0 0 var(--r-md) 0;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: 11.5px;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    html[data-page="BL"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; }

    /* ── SHARED MOBILE PASS · 760 / 520 ────────────────────────────────────── */
    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      /* The MAX is the BASE clamp's own value at 760px (31.00px), not a round
         number. Anything higher and the headline GROWS as the viewport narrows
         past 761 — base clamp(31px,4vw,54px) bottoms out around there, so a max of 38-42
         was landing ABOVE where the curve arrived from. It is a jump no
         screenshot at 1440 or 375 can show you: it lives in the one pixel
         either side of the boundary. The vw term is untouched, so the steeper
         small-screen curve this breakpoint exists for still happens. */
      html[data-page="BL"] :where(.h2) { font-size: clamp(27px,7.2vw,31px); max-width: none; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      html[data-page="BL"] :where(.lede) { max-width: none; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 520px) {
      html[data-page="BL"] :where(.kick) { font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: .3em; }
      html[data-page="BL"] :where(.btn) { padding: 15px 24px; }
    }
</style>

<style is:inline set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
{visibility.headerSection !== false && <HeaderBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
<main id="main">
  {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBL content={content} layout={layout} />}
</main>
{visibility.footerSection !== false && <FooterBL content={content} layout={layout} />}

<script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var els = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
    if (!els.length) return;
    if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window) ||
        window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
      els.forEach(function (el) { el.classList.add('in'); });
      return;
    }
    var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      entries.forEach(function (e) {
        if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(e.target); }
      });
    }, { rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px', threshold: 0.06 });
    els.forEach(function (el) { io.observe(el); });
  })();

  // Family-unique name — LocationBL calls this exact string. The innerHTML wipe
  // is what erases the drawn fallback map-face before Leaflet paints. The short
  // retry covers a slow or blocked CDN and gives up rather than spinning: the
  // drawn face IS the design and is a perfectly good thing to be left with.
  window.__foodcraftBLInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
    var tries = 0;
    (function go() {
      var el = document.getElementById('map');
      if (!el) return;
      if (typeof window.L === 'undefined') {
        if (tries++ < 25) setTimeout(go, 80);
        return;
      }
      el.innerHTML = '';
      var map = window.L.map(el, { scrollWheelZoom: false, attributionControl: true }).setView([lat, lng], 16);
      // LABELLED basemap: someone finding a café needs the street names, and
      // voyager is the CARTO set that sits inside a warm cream design.
      window.L.tileLayer('https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/voyager/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', {
        maxZoom: 19, subdomains: 'abcd',
        attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO',
      }).addTo(map);
      // Colours are READ from the live tokens rather than baked, so an admin
      // colour pick recolours the pin too.
      var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
      var accent = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent') || '').trim() || '#B4541F';
      var paper = (cs.getPropertyValue('--paper') || '').trim() || '#FFFCF6';
      var icon = window.L.divIcon({
        className: '',
        iconSize: [16, 16], iconAnchor: [8, 8],
        html: '<span style="display:block;width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:' +
              accent + ';border:3px solid ' + paper + ';box-shadow:0 0 0 1px ' + accent + '"></span>',
      });
      var marker = window.L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon }).addTo(map);
      if (label) marker.bindPopup(label);
    })();
  };
</script>
</body>
</html>
